From 7ef5ebee7799fbdbe379e7ff675b744f25bfdcb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:00:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] drivers: display: add jadard jd9365 mipi-dsi panel driver

Add support for the Jadard JD9365 MIPI-DSI panel controller. The driver
performs the vendor initialisation sequence over DCS, attaches to the host
in video burst mode, and drives the reset and backlight pins. Pixels are
streamed by the display controller the panel is wired to, so the driver
reports the panel geometry and handles blanking only -- the same shape as
the EK79007 driver it is modelled on.

The initialisation table is the vendor sequence for the Waveshare 10.1in
800x1280 2-lane module, transcribed from Espressif's esp_lcd_jd9365
component as republished in waveshareteam/Waveshare-ESP32-components. That
table hardcodes the DSI lane register, so the replay loop tracks the
register page and substitutes the devicetree lane count instead, which
keeps data-lanes from being a property that silently does nothing.

The panel has GS/SS mirror bits but no transpose, so set_orientation
accepts only DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_NORMAL.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
